# Commit messages

When the user asks for a commit, draft the message from the staged diff. Follow `prompts/commit-message.md`.

## Format

```
<type>: <why this change exists>

- <area or file>: <what changed>
```

## Types

- `feature` — new behavior
- `fix` — bug fix
- `refactor` — behavior-preserving restructure
- `test` — tests only
- `docs` — documentation only
- `chore` — tooling, dependencies, or repo maintenance

## Rules

- Lead with why, in one sentence.
- Name each area or file that changed. Keep the body to the point.
- Match the tone of recent `git log` messages when history exists.
- Do not commit unless the user explicitly asks.

```
feature: keep session tokens on the server

- auth/session.ts: sign tokens only in the server action
- app/login/page.tsx: stop returning the token to the client
```
